{"path":"ranges/cartesian_product_view/iterator/iter_move","title":"iter_move(ranges::cartesian_product_view::iterator)","titleHtml":"iter_move<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">(ranges::cartesian_product_view::<i>iterator</i>)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/cartesian_product_view/iterator/iter_move","section":"ranges","kind":"page","summary":"Let current_ be the underlying tuple of iterators.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">friend</span> <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> iter_move<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*iterator*/</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> i <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/* see below */</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Let <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/cartesian_product_view/iterator#Data_members\"><code><i>current_</i></code></a> be the underlying tuple of iterators.\n</p><p>Equivalent to: <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*tuple-transform*/</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/ranges/iter_move\"><span class=\"kw3158\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iter_move</span></span></a>, i.<span class=\"me1\">current_</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>\n</p><p>This function  is not visible to ordinary <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/unqualified_lookup\">unqualified</a> or <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/qualified_lookup\">qualified lookup</a>, and can only be found by <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/adl\">argument-dependent lookup</a> when <code>cartesian_product_view::<i>iterator</i>&lt;Const&gt;</code> is an associated class of the arguments.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> i\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> iterator\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A tuple that contains the result of applying <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/ranges/iter_move\"><span class=\"kw3158\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iter_move</span></span></a></span></code> to the stored underlying iterators converted to the return type, as described above.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>The exception specification is equivalent to the logical AND of the following expressions:\n</p>\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/ranges/iter_move\"><span class=\"kw3158\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iter_move</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">get</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>N<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i.<span class=\"me1\">current_</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> for every integer <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">0</span> ≤ N ≤ sizeof...<span class=\"br0\">(</span>Vs<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>,\n</li><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_move_constructible\"><span class=\"kw550\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_nothrow_move_constructible_v</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range_reference_t\"><span class=\"kw2914\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">range_rvalue_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*maybe-const*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Const, T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span></span></code> for every type <code>T</code> in <code>First, Vs...</code>.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/ranges/iter_move\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>iter_move</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td> casts the result of dereferencing an object to its associated rvalue reference type<br><span class=\"t-mark\">(customization point object)</span></td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"ranges","title":"Ranges library (since C++20)"},{"path":"ranges/cartesian_product_view","title":"std::ranges::views::cartesian_product, std::ranges::cartesian_product_view"},{"path":"ranges/cartesian_product_view/iterator","title":"std::ranges::cartesian_product_view<First, Vs...>::iterator"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"iter_move(ranges::cartesian_product_view::iterator)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++23. Let current_ be the underlying tuple of iterators."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"i"},{"label":"Return value","note":"A tuple that contains the result of applying ranges::iter_move to the stored underlying iterators converted to the return type, as described above."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"The exception specification is equivalent to the logical AND of the following expressions:"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"iter_move","note":"casts the result of dereferencing an object to its 